@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose Lowers type-checked AST into a linear SSA-style IR (flat temps, struct-offset layout), then emits LLVM IR text for clang. Effects and errors erase at codegen; GC roots are pinned to a per-function stack frame.
@depends [parser, resolver, checker, diagnostic]

---

@workflow full_compile
@purpose source file -> native binary
@steps
  1. generate_from_source: lex -> resolve -> check -> lower -> LLVM IR -> clang -> binary. Stops at the first passing-phase failure. [src: codegen.aria:19-42]
  2. lower() is the multi-pass heart: const/string collection, body lowering, trampolines, derives, monomorphization. [src: lower.aria:19634-19641]
  3. generate_llvm_ir_to_file writes the .ll and invokes clang with runtime.c. [src: codegen.aria:49-75]

@workflow lower_pipeline
@purpose Typed AST -> IrModule
@steps
  1. _scan_consts collects const and string literals into module-level tables. [src: lower.aria:19636]
  2. _lower_bodies runs three sub-passes: struct layout (field offsets), fn signatures (FnSig), body -> SSA IR. [src: lower.aria:937]
  3. _lower_trampolines emits vtable-dispatch stubs for trait methods. [src: lower.aria:19638]
  4. _lower_derives synthesises Eq/Ord/... trait impls. [src: lower.aria:19639]
  5. _lower_mono_pass inlines generic monomorphizations discovered during lowering. [src: lower.aria:19640]

@workflow llvm_emission
@purpose IrFunc -> LLVM IR text
@steps
  1. _build_gc_tables pre-computes is_root[temp] + slot[temp] for every GC root in a single O(insts + temps) pass. [src: llvm.aria:269]
  2. alloca i64 per temp (LLVM mem2reg collapses redundant loads/stores downstream). [src: llvm.aria:1140-1143]
  3. Reserve GC frame on stack: [prev_ptr, count, roots...] (2 + gc_root_count i64 slots); zero roots via llvm.memset intrinsic. [src: llvm.aria:1168-1180]
  4. _gen_inst dispatches per op, emits LLVM text into a [str] parts array, tracks last_was_term to elide fallthrough labels. [src: llvm.aria:1206-1210]
  5. _join tree-merges parts into final text in O(L log N) — replaces the original O(L^2) chain-concat that memcpy'd hundreds of GB on large programs. [src: llvm.aria:24-54]

---

@invariants
  Every instruction produces a numbered SSA temp in [0, local_count); no re-assignment. [src: ir.aria:6, lower.aria:20]
  Struct field access uses OpFieldGet/Set with a flat (pre-computed) offset; never recursive layout resolution at codegen time. [src: lower.aria:12658-12681]
  Result layout: tag at slot 0, payload after (2-3 slots total). Strings are (ptr, len) pairs (2 slots). [src: lower.aria:1171-1185, lower.aria:352]
  GC roots are cached on LlvmGen at function entry; no per-instruction recomputation. [src: llvm.aria:157-158, llvm.aria:269]
  String constants are module-scoped; ConstStr insts reference string_constants[idx]. [src: ir.aria:245-267]
  Function lookup uses binary search over sorted fn_index_keys — critical for bootstrapping speed. [src: ir.aria:384-402]

---

@antipatterns
  Linear scan for fn lookup in mod_find_func: once-upon-a-time O(N) per call, invoked once per OpCall. On self-host (~100K calls, ~1K functions) this was 100M string comparisons. Binary search cut it to ~1M. Do NOT re-introduce linear scan in this path. [src: ir.aria:237-244]
  Per-instruction GC-root recomputation via _is_gc_root: was O(temps x insts) per function, dominated 95% of codegen CPU for token_name. Caching via _build_gc_tables reduces to O(1) lookups. [src: llvm.aria:188-192, llvm.aria:266-268]
  Chained string concat in _join: the obvious implementation is O(L^2) for a ~50MB LLVM text; tree-merge join gets O(L log N). [src: llvm.aria:23-29]
  Initializing GC frame one slot at a time: 2 LLVM instructions per root, O(gc_root_count) per function entry. Using the memset intrinsic collapses it to 1 call — for token_name alone this dropped from ~90M to ~1M emitted instructions. [src: llvm.aria:1172-1180]

